            <ArticleTitle>Model mis-specification and overestimation of the intraclass correlation coefficient in cluster randomized trials.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>957-64</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intraclass correlation coefficient (ICC) estimates must be provided when reporting the results of a cluster randomized trial. This study demonstrates that estimating this parameter with one-way ANOVA and an underlying mixed-effects statistical model leads to biased estimates. The bias depends on the effect size of the studied treatment.</AbstractText>
